-- statement:
--   **One line through the seven passes is `lineB`.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegSw3`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.pipeLine_eq (hl : 1 ≤ lam) (hst : s ≤ t) (hN : nc * lam = t)
--       (hG : (LJ s t lam w).length ≤ G) (y : List (ℤ × ℤ)) :
--       let N := nc * lam
--       let S := slabLine N (selSrc s t) (selH p P) y
--       let Y := chunksG (fun q => liftG (chunkK P R s t lam α q)) lam nc S
--       let Jl := slabLine G (jSrc s t lam w) (fun _ z => z) Y
--       let W := liftG (jKer P R s t lam w α K G) Jl
--       let Wp := slabLine N (scSrc s t lam w) (fun _ z => z) W
--       let Y2 := chunksG (fun q => liftG (chunkK P R s t lam α q)) lam nc Wp
--       slabLine N (fun l => some l) (outH p P s t α) (List.zip Y Y2) =
--         lineB p P R s t lam w α K nc y
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** B-line machine, sweep 3: the `B₀` axis map as seven passes
--
--   On a `(pre, N, post)` array of Gaussian items (`N = n_c λ`), the in-place `B₀` line map of the
--   axis (`axisL N post (lineB …)`) is computed by (`axisPipe`):
--
--   1. a selection slab pass (row `rowSel l`, scaled by `2^{P-p-1}`, zeros for `l ≥ s`);
--   2. the chunk kernel `chunkK` on every `λ`-chunk (one `λ`-exposure);
--   3. a slab gather of the `m` near-boundary rows `LJ` (padded to `G` rows);
--   4. the `J` kernel (`fwdK`, `bwdK`, coupling window) on every `G`-row (one `G`-exposure);
--   5. a slab scatter back to the `N` rows;
--   6. the chunk kernel again;
--   7. the output slab pass on the pair `(Y, Y₂)`: `outE l (Y - Y₂)`.
--
--   Real and imaginary parts are carried together (`liftG`). **`axisPipe_eq`** proves the equality.
